BPASS test subset
=================

A small subset of the BPASS v2.2.1 stellar models at Z = 0.014 (z014), used by
tests/test_be_physics.py so that physics tests on real BPASS tracks can run
without the full (~13 GB) release.

Contents (in the release's own folder layout):
  NEWSINMODS/z014/            single stars of 1, 5, 20 and 60 Msun (compared with
                              MIST), plus the single stars that the binaries'
                              companions continue onto
  NEWBINMODS/NEWBINMODS/z014/ three binaries with M1 = 10 Msun: one merger, one
                              rejuvenated companion and one plain (disrupted) system;
                              plus a 5 Msun merger whose secondary column ticks up
                              while it is absorbed (5-0.9-0.2)

Each file keeps only the leading columns that arsenal_gear reads (6 for single
stars, 49 for binaries), copied as text so the values are unchanged.
Regenerate with: python tests/data/make_bpass_fixture.py [BPASS_ROOTDIR]

These files are for testing only. When using BPASS, cite:
  Eldridge, Stanway et al. 2017, PASA, 34, e058 (doi:10.1017/pasa.2017.51)
  Stanway & Eldridge 2018, MNRAS, 479, 75 (doi:10.1093/mnras/sty1353)
